{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1164 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "7f2ad23505a41c140b414be45d1dd8f0e5a5f9da21a31bc180b200fc0488f79f" :edb/db-before-t 1163 :edb/db-after-t 1164 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534476 50 #inst "2026-10-11T21:54:37.735Z" 13194139534476 17592186045417 true] [17592186237950 1071 "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-2y=4 \\\\ 6=5x\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534476 17592186045417 true] [17592186237950 1071 "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4x-2y=4 \\\\ 6=5x\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534476 17592186045417 false] [17592186237950 1074 "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-2y=4 \\\\ 5x=6.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 0-5\\cdot (-2)}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534476 17592186045417 true] [17592186237950 1074 "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4x-2y=4 \\\\ 5x=6.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 0-5\\cdot (-2)}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534476 17592186045417 false] [17592186287751 1074 "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set\n\n$$\nS=R\\times R\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is any real number and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number.\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in R,\\,y\\in R\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{0}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $0$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{0}=\\{(0,y)\\,:\\,y\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{0}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/07/07a3d9a6c38b5bfcc529496735a1a66eaceefd5ae3437a2cb0cd45911eccafae.png)\n\nNow, consider a general ${S}_{i}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals some $i\\in R$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{i}=\\{(i,y)\\,:\\,y\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nFor each $i\\in R,$ ${S}_{i}$ is a vertical line.\n\n![](images/e4/e454f1cf125486ca25acf15e26efd251a4a03b08e899814ab3e77db7898713c4.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product $S$ is the union of these subsets over $R:$\n\n$$\nS={⋃}_{i\\in R}{S}_{i}.\n$$\n\nThis is the whole plane, as shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/07/070389fcdb6d69f9aa90dabbd98a0d3461e26d3e3e08b1d53b92e99688c09923.png)" 13194139534476 17592186045417 true] [17592186287751 1074 "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set\n\n$$\nS=R\\times R\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is any real number and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number.\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in R,\\,y\\in R}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{0}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $0$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{0}={(0,y)\\,:\\,y\\in R}\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{0}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/07/07a3d9a6c38b5bfcc529496735a1a66eaceefd5ae3437a2cb0cd45911eccafae.png)\n\nNow, consider a general ${S}_{i}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals some $i\\in R$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{i}={(i,y)\\,:\\,y\\in R}\n$$\n\nFor each $i\\in R,$ ${S}_{i}$ is a vertical line.\n\n![](images/e4/e454f1cf125486ca25acf15e26efd251a4a03b08e899814ab3e77db7898713c4.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product $S$ is the union of these subsets over $R:$\n\n$$\nS={⋃}_{i\\in R}{S}_{i}.\n$$\n\nThis is the whole plane, as shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/07/070389fcdb6d69f9aa90dabbd98a0d3461e26d3e3e08b1d53b92e99688c09923.png)" 13194139534476 17592186045417 false] [17592186416139 1074 "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{2}+1 \\\\  & 2{x}^{2}-2x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}-\\phantom{8}x+7\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2{x}^{2}-x+7 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\,2{x}^{2}-2x+1}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nAs a result,\n\n- the quotient is $3{x}^{2}+1,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $x+6.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{6{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}-x+7}{2{x}^{2}-2x+1}=3{x}^{2}+1+\\frac{x+6}{2{x}^{2}-2x+1}.\n$$" 13194139534476 17592186045417 true] [17592186416139 1074 "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{2}+1 \\\\  & 2{x}^{2}-2x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}-x+7\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2{x}^{2}-x+7 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\,2{x}^{2}-2x+1}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nAs a result,\n\n- the quotient is $3{x}^{2}+1,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $x+6.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{6{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}-x+7}{2{x}^{2}-2x+1}=3{x}^{2}+1+\\frac{x+6}{2{x}^{2}-2x+1}.\n$$" 13194139534476 17592186045417 false]] :edb/tempids {}}
